[2026-09-27 18:33:16] [MODULE] Hero wave separator + line-art botanical — Reworked the landing hero curve and corner decoration. The separator between the hero copy panel and the photo was .home-hero-copy::before using 'border-radius: 0 55% 55% 0', which is a single uniform elliptical arc - exactly the 'plain circular curve' symptom. Replaced it with a mask-image wave: the silhouette is now a five-segment cubic path (M0,0 H90 C76,150 98,300 87,420 C76,540 97,700 88,820 C84,898 90,958 90,1000) so the edge undulates in and out along its height. The mask lives in two custom properties (--home-wave-right and --home-wave-bottom) declared on .home-hero, so the panel and the gold lining stay in lockstep and the 900px breakpoint swaps both from one place. Used a mask rather than an inline SVG shape specifically so the fill stays on 'background' and therefore on the --color-soft token, and so the existing 900px/600px media queries that reposition the panel (left/top/width/height) keep working untouched. Added .home-hero-edge, an inline stroked SVG of the identical path, to carry the gold lining that the old border-right provided; it uses vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke so the 1.5px line stays 1.5px under the preserveAspectRatio=none stretch, and it is display:none below 900px matching the old 'border-right: 0' behaviour. Responsiveness: both mask paths carry preserveAspectRatio=none with mask-size 100% 100%, so the wave scales with the resolved column width instead of letterboxing, and the 900px query swaps to the bottom-right wave that replaced the old 'border-radius: 0 0 55% 0' mobile arc. For the corner decoration, replaced the two filled Unicode florettes (&#10048;, 105px, text-gold-light, opacity 0.43) with line-art botanical SVGs: a five-petal blossom with a stem and two leaves built from strokes only (fill=none, stroke=currentColor, stroke-width 1.25), sized 300px top-left and 190px bottom, coloured rgb(var(--color-gold-light)) at 0.5 and 0.34 opacity. Converted the