[2026-09-27 22:06:54] [MODULE] Admin Gates — Fixed TypeError blanking every admin screen: AppServiceProvider defined each admin.* Gate with a ?Admin parameter, but Gate passes the *default* guard's user, and the default guard is the customer web guard, so any admin signed in alongside a customer session got a User handed to a ?Admin parameter and fataled before the closure body ran. Changed the parameter to untyped with a null default, which keeps Gate willing to evaluate for a guest while letting the body read the admin guard (which it already did, overwriting the argument). Added AdminLayoutTest::test_the_panel_renders_for_an_admin_who_is_also_signed_in_as_a_customer, which uses Auth::guard('admin')->setUser() rather than actingAs() because actingAs() calls shouldUse() and would move the default guard, hiding the collision.
