[2026-09-28 06:07:10] [MODULE] Calendar Blocking (MCA parity) — Ported MCA Cafe's reservation-calendar blocking process onto the Calendar and Blocked Dates page, keeping BTA's design language. Schema: new migration adds a nullable string(5) 'time' to blocked_dates, mirroring MCA's own add_time_to_blocked_dates_table. Null means all day, so every pre-existing block stays a full-day block and nothing needs rewriting. Model: time added to fillable, plus isPartialDay(), isSalonWide() and a time_label accessor (1:30 PM / All day). Controller: store() now validates time as nullable date_format:H:i, persists it, and adds after_or_equal:today on start_date so a past date is refused server-side as well as being greyed out in the grid. Grid: every day is now a button; past days and the neighbouring-month spill-over get the disabled attribute with disabled:opacity-40, and hover styles moved to enabled:hover: because CSS :hover still matches a disabled button. Clickable days carry title='Block <date>' and dispatch a block-date window event, since the cells sit outside the dialog's Alpine scope; the dialog seeds date from old(start_date) and x-model owns the field. Modal: Date (pre-filled, editable), End Date (optional), Services, Time (optional), Reason, then Cancel / Block, in BTA's form components and button styles. Blocked Dates is now a table in MCA's column order - Date, Services, Time, Reason, Action - with the scope shown as a legend-coloured dot plus a badge, and the action renamed to Mark Available. The legend is unchanged and blocked cells keep the cancelled background with a primary dot for salon-wide and a gold dot for service-specific, now with the time in the tooltip.
