[2026-09-28 06:14:59] [MODULE] Calendar Blocking (MCA parity) — Fixed 'The end date cannot be before the start date.' rejecting a single-day block. Three compounding causes. (1) The dialog form is novalidate, so the browser never stopped an end date that preceded the start. (2) The end date's min was pinned to $firstBookable, a fixed date, so the picker happily offered days before the chosen start - a regression from the original card, which used old(start_date). (3) A stale end_date carried back through old() could contradict a freshly clicked day. The message itself is also used verbatim by PromoController for ends_at/starts_at, so if it reappears on the Promos form that is a separate field pair - worth asking which form they hit. Fixed at both ends: BlockedDate::booted() now collapses an end_date that is not strictly after start_date down to start_date, next to the blank-end_date collapse that already existed, because a start and end on the same day is already how a single-day block is stored and an earlier end is not a range anyone can act on; CalendarController::store() drops the after_or_equal:start_date rule and its message, keeping the past-date rule. In the dialog, end_date is now Alpine-bound with x-bind:min tracking the picked day, and picking a new day clears an end date that would now precede it.
