[2026-09-28 22:30:39] [MODULE] Font Awesome webfont path fix — Root cause of the FA icons not showing: not the icon syntax. Vite's default base of '/' wrote root-absolute url(/build/assets/fa-solid-900-*.woff2) into the compiled CSS, but the app is served from htdocs/BTA/public rather than the domain root, so the browser requested http://localhost/build/assets/... and got a 404. The webfont never loaded, so every FA icon rendered as an empty box. Fixed by setting base: './' in vite.config.js so url() resolves against the CSS file's own location; the reference is now ./fa-solid-900-IAB4Droh.woff2 and all four woff2 files return 200 from /BTA/public/build/assets/. Verified the full chain in the built CSS rather than by fetching the path I assumed was correct, which is what fooled me last turn: .fas sets font-family, :is(.fas...):before injects content:var(--fa), .fa-sign-in-alt resolves to U+F2F6, .fa-solid sets weight 900, the solid-900 @font-face points at the relative URL, and zero url(/build/...) references remain. Comment in vite.config.js explains why the relative base is required. This was a pre-existing config gap that only surfaced now because the webfont is the first asset referenced from inside CSS by url(). 144 tests pass.
