[2026-09-29 00:28:38] [MODULE] Booking rules + admin calendar — Implemented the five-part booking/calendar brief. (1) Booking starts tomorrow: BookingAvailability::firstBookableDate() is now today()->addDay() and dateProblems() returns MINIMUM_NOTICE_MESSAGE for today and the past; both customer form requests override failedValidation to flash an amber toast for that message and for BLOCKED_MESSAGE. The date input's min is bound to Alpine state that mirrors firstBookableDate, so the grey-out follows the server instead of being a second hardcoded value. (2) Accept flow: only status=confirmed appointments are queried for the calendar cells, so pending ones stay in the Appointments list; no per-day cap was added. Blocking is now category-scoped - a new blocked_dates.service_category column replaces the per-service scope in the dialog, with the old column retained for legacy rows; blockedRanges() matches a service, its category, or salon-wide, and a booking on a blocked date is rejected server-side. Blocking a day that already holds pending or confirmed appointments returns a confirm_block flash that opens the dialog on a Block-anyway step; the controller re-counts so the warning cannot be understated by posting force=1, and nothing existing is ever cancelled. (3) Toasts: new x-ui.toast and x-ui.toast-stack components, mounted in both layouts outside @stack('modals') so a toast outlives the dialog that raised it. Server flashes and a window event both feed the same stack; 4s dismissal, 300ms fade, dismissible button. Wired to block, mark-available, accept, decline, and the two date rules. (4) Cell display: chips tinted with the category colour and labelled in a darker shade, max 3 then a '+N more' link to the day's appointments; Blocked chips stay in the existing cancelled styling and do not borrow a category colour; cells grow with the busiest day. (5) Legend: one row above the grid, right-aligned, one swatch per category, colours read from the database. Created a real service_categories table (migration backfills the 11 existing category strings and links services to them) plus App\Models\ServiceCategory, an admin Categories screen at /admin/categories with a swatch picker, and a sidebar entry. Category colours come from the stored column; a saving hook on Service creates a missing category row so a typed category can never fall out of the legend. Two real bugs found and fixed along the way: blockedRanges() treated any null service_id as salon-wide, so a category block also closed every other service until the salon-wide branch tested both columns; and the palette lookup only trimmed a trailing noun once, so 'Bleaching' and 'Hair Care' silently consumed palette slots instead of matching 'Bleaching Services' and 'Hair Care Services'. Added tests/Feature/BookingRulesTest.php (34 tests) covering all five areas, and updated the range-era assertions in CalendarBlockingTest and AdminLayoutTest. All six requested checks pass.
