[2026-10-01 10:32:14] [MODULE] Cross-Tab Session Sync — Fixed both reported bugs in the single-active-role cross-tab sync.  BUG 1 root cause (server): both guards share one session cookie, so Laravel's single url.intended was written by whichever guard bounced a guest and read by whichever login ran next. A guest bounced off /dashboard left that URL behind, so POST /admin/login sent the staff member to the CUSTOMER dashboard, which then 302'd to /login - a successful sign-in that looked broken. Added App\Support\IntendedUrl (guard-scoped key bta.intended.<scope>, read-and-clear, same-origin check) and hooked the write into the two places that actually redirect a guest: AuthenticateCustomer (new, extends the framework Authenticate) and AuthenticateAdmin. Both login controllers now use IntendedUrl::pull() instead of redirect()->intended(). Note: route middleware listed before auth is sorted BEHIND auth by SortedMiddleware and never runs, which is why the hook lives in an Authenticate subclass.  BUG 2 root cause (client): sessionSync in resources/js/app.js treated localStorage as authoritative over the server-rendered bta-session meta tag, and on load, when they disagreed, it navigated to the stored value and returned early - never re-announcing, never repairing the stale value, and never attaching the storage listener. A stale value therefore survived every page load, so a tab that had just logged out was dragged back to /dashboard, /dashboard bounced to /login, and it looped forever. That is the blinking. Rewrote the module around one rule: the meta tag is the only authority for this page, localStorage is a noticeboard. Load now announces unconditionally and never navigates. Navigation happens only on another tab's storage event or a visibility catch-up, budgeted to one hop per identity via sessionStorage; unrecognised values are repaired instead of followed (that path used to be location.replace(location.href), an unbounded self-reload); null newValue is ignored; the bfcache probe now compares the guard only, since /session-status reports a guard and no id and comparing it against admin:3 disagreed with itself on every Back press.  Also: added bta-session-status meta to all three layouts - the probe was hardcoded to /session-status, which 404s under the htdocs/BTA/public subdirectory install.  Tests: 7 new cases in SingleActiveRoleTest covering the cross-guard redirect both ways, same-guard destination still honoured, destination not reused, the full reported sequence, and source-level assertions pinning announce-on-load/no-navigate-on-load and the one-hop budget.
