[2026-10-01 12:28:23] [MODULE] Item 4 - Profile picture crop — Added a crop step before a profile picture is saved, ported from MCACAFE_v1's pattern. Same library: Cropper.js v1.6.2, vendored into public/vendor/cropper/ (copied from the reference project, not an npm range, so the version is pinned by a file and cannot drift). Same UX: pick a file, a draggable square crop box opens, Apply Crop writes the cropped canvas back into the file input via DataTransfer, Cancel backs out, and the upload itself is unchanged - the form still posts profile_photo and the user still presses Save, so nothing is sent until then and Cancel genuinely cancels. 1:1 aspect ratio at 500x500 output, matching the reference.  DEVIATION from the reference, deliberate: the modal shell is BTA's own x-ui.dialog (new resources/views/components/ui/photo-crop-dialog.blade.php) rather than a Bootstrap modal. BTA has no Bootstrap at all, so copying those markup and inline styles in would have imported a dependency to render one dialog. The cropper's own stylesheet and the library itself are the vendored files; everything else is the house Tailwind component.  The cropper is loaded per-view via @push('head')/@push('scripts') rather than bundled - 37 KB on every page for one dialog is not worth it. Alpine component 'profilePhotoCrop' does nothing until a file is chosen and declines quietly if window.Cropper is missing, so a failed asset load leaves the picker working uncropped instead of breaking it. The cropper is built only after the dialog is visible ( + requestAnimationFrame) because it measures its container and the dialog is x-show driven - built while closed it comes up zero-sized.  Two bugs found and fixed on the way: heroicon-o-crop does not exist in blade-heroicons and naming it 500'd the whole profile page - used heroicon-o-viewfinder-circle instead, which is a better fit anyway. And the camera badge pointed at for='profile_photo' (the field NAME) while x-ui.form.input rendered id='', so it labelled no control at all; the input now has the real id the label and the cropper both use.  ADMIN PROFILE SKIPPED per the request's own condition ('if it has a similar picture upload field'). It does not: admin/profile/edit.blade.php has no avatar or file input, AdminProfileController has no photo handling, and the admin topbar renders initials unconditionally. The admins table does have a profile_photo_path column and the model lists it as fillable, so it is a small follow-up if wanted - but that is new feature work, not applying a crop to an existing field.  New tests/Feature/ProfilePhotoCropTest.php (11 cases) pins the vendored version, that only the profile page loads it, the scope/dialog/id wiring, that the label is really associated with the input, both buttons being type=button so they cannot submit the profile form, the square 500x500 output, the after-open construction, the DataTransfer write-back, and that a cropped PNG upload is accepted by the server.
