. 2. If using `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` + `storage` event: - Confirm that on login/logout, a shared key (e.g., `auth_session_version` or `active_user_id`) is actually being WRITTEN to localStorage so other tabs can detect the change. - Confirm the `storage` event listener is actually registered on page load in every tab, and that the handler correctly triggers a reload or redirect when it fires. - Common bug: forgetting that `storage` events do NOT fire in the SAME tab that made the change — only in other tabs. If the implementation is only writing the key but never actually listening for the event (or listening incorrectly), other tabs will never react. 3. If a polling/AJAX approach is preferred instead (more reliable across all browsers): - Implement a lightweight periodic check (e.g., every 5-10 seconds) from each open tab to a backend endpoint (e.g., /api/session-check) that returns the CURRENT actively logged-in user's ID/role from the server session. - Compare this against the tab's last-known user ID/role (stored in a JS variable on page load). - If they differ, automatically reload the page (or redirect to the appropriate dashboard/home for the new role) without requiring the user to manually refresh. 4. Test this exact sequence after the fix and confirm it works: a. Tab A: log in as customer "Ruciel". Confirm navbar shows "Ruciel". b. Open Tab B: confirm it also shows "Ruciel" (same active session). c. Tab B: log out, log in as admin "Maia Arjud". Confirm Tab B shows "Maia Arjud" and loads the admin dashboard correctly (no 500 error, per the earlier bug fix). d. WITHOUT refreshing Tab A manually, switch back to it and WAIT a few seconds — Tab A must automatically update on its own to show "Maia Arjud" / the admin view, with NO manual refresh required. e. Repeat in reverse (log out of admin, log in as a different customer in Tab B) and confirm Tab A automatically picks up that change too. 5. Make sure this automatic update does not cause a reload loop or flickering (a known issue from the earlier implementation attempt) — only trigger a reload when the session/user ACTUALLY changes compared to what that tab last knew, not on every check. Report back which mechanism was used (storage event vs. polling) and confirm the full test sequence above passes with NO manual refresh needed in Tab A.
