TIONS on the price field (e.g., calculating booking totals, down payments, balance due). Since prices can now be non-numeric strings like "100+" or "249/499": - For booking/checkout purposes, you likely still need an actual numeric base price to calculate totals. Flag this back to me — we may need a separate numeric "base_price" field (used for actual calculations at checkout) alongside this new flexible "display_price" string field (used only for showing the price list to browsing customers, e.g., on the Services page). Do not silently break booking total calculations — confirm this approach with me before implementing, or implement both fields if the direction is clear enough from this description. Apply this across the Services management (admin), Services display (customer-facing), and confirm booking/checkout flow still correctly calculates totals using actual numeric values where required.
