[2026-10-01 20:21:41] [MODULE] Dev server startup — Fixed the recurring 'Firefox can't connect to 127.0.0.1:8000' error. Root cause: dev-up.bat treated the marker file storage/dev-server.ready as proof the site was up, but that file survives a crash/reboot, so every run after an unclean shutdown skipped the wait and opened the browser onto a dead port. New tools/wait-for-site.ps1 polls http://127.0.0.1:8000/ for a real HTTP response; dev-up.bat and start-dev.bat now use it and clear the stale marker first. dev-up.bat no longer opens the browser at all if the site never comes up. Also pinned --host/--port in start-dev.bat so artisan serve cannot fall back to 8001, cleared the stale marker on supervisor startup, and unblocked the supervisor's health probe so the ready marker appears immediately instead of after 120s.
