[2026-10-02 04:04:37] [MODULE] Admin Terms version history + bulk select-all fix — Two fixes. (1) Removed the Version History block from the admin Terms index (resources/views/admin/terms/index.blade.php): the per-version rows with Edit/Preview/Publish/Delete. Kept a single Preview link on each policy card, because the Preview lived inside that block and removing it wholesale would have left the admin with no way to see the customer-facing rendering at all - the raw textarea is not what a customer reads. (2) Fixed the broken select-all. Root cause found in the browser console: 'Alpine Expression Error: notificationBulk is not defined' on 'appointmentBulk()'. app.js registered the alias as Alpine.data('appointmentBulk', () => notificationBulk()), but Alpine.data('notificationBulk', ...) registers a NAME and never binds a variable, so the factory threw a ReferenceError the moment either screen mounted it and produced an EMPTY scope. Nothing on the page said so: the header checkbox is a real input and the browser ticks it regardless, so the customer saw a select-all box that filled in precisely nothing. Affected admin/appointments/archived and customer/appointments/index (both used the alias); the notifications list was fine because it asks for notificationBulk() by name. Fixed by extracting the factory to a named const bulkSelection() and registering both names from it, so they cannot drift again. Also added the someSelected getter, which customer/appointments/index.blade.php already bound with x-bind:indeterminate but which did not exist in the component, producing a second console error.
